  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "How many ways can six differently coloured balls be distributed among three bins so that",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "at least one of these bins is empty?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$189$ ways.\n\nUse inclusion–exclusion on the three empty-bin events.",
          "worked": "Let $A$, $B$ and $C$ be the distributions in which the first, second and third bins, respectively, are empty. Each ball has two choices when one specified bin is empty, and one choice when two specified bins are empty. All three bins cannot be empty.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|A|=|B|=|C|&=2^6=64\\\\|A\\cap B|=|A\\cap C|=|B\\cap C|&=1\\\\|A\\cap B\\cap C|&=0\\\\|A\\cup B\\cup C|&=3\\times64-3\\times1+0\\\\|A\\cup B\\cup C|&=189\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "no bin is empty?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$540$ ways.\n\nSubtract the distributions with an empty bin from all distributions.",
          "worked": "Each of the six balls has three choices of bin. Subtract the distributions counted in part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=3^6-189\\\\N&=729-189\\\\N&=540\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
